// A dip, a fenced ember, two origins three cells apart on a chasm floor whose echoes cross into one bar; a long road with a dip and a fenced ember beyond.
name Two Echoes
rule B1357/S1357
steps 2
hint Two seeds, one chasm, one shape. Two echoes crossed here, close enough to touch. Plant where they must have started, climb out on the boulder to the right, and Grow.
tip Two generations of echo from one origin leave three cells in a row, two rows above it, one cell apart. Two of those overlapping make the bar of four. The origins are three cells apart on the chasm floor, under the bar.
intro Two origins, close enough to touch. Their echoes crossed, and where they crossed the shape is one that neither would make alone.
outro Two beginnings, one shape. Nothing that grows keeps its own edges.
